# Database safety guard configuration.
#
# NON-SECRET and committed on purpose. This file contains no credentials - only
# the identity of the Neon endpoint that Phase 1 development work is allowed to
# touch. It is read by scripts/db-guard.mjs.
#
# This is deliberately NOT in .env: .env holds credentials and is gitignored, so
# a safety rule placed there would not be shared, reviewed, or version-controlled.
#
# EDP_DB_EXPECT_HOST is the Neon endpoint id of the phase1-development branch.
# The guard refuses to run any Prisma database command unless the first DNS label
# of the resolved hostname is exactly this value, or this value with a "-pooler"
# suffix. An environment variable of the same name overrides this file.
EDP_DB_EXPECT_HOST=ep-young-moon-azdhrnrr
